# Docker build context trimming.
#
# `augur build` runs `docker build "$SCRIPT_DIR"`, where $SCRIPT_DIR is the install dir
# (~/.augur) for an installed augur, or this repo for a dev build. The Dockerfile installs
# everything over the network (it has NO COPY/ADD), so the build context is UNUSED — yet
# Docker still tars the whole dir and ships it to the daemon. Without this file the macOS
# VM disk images under ~/.augur/vms (tens of GB) get swept in, ballooning the context to
# 17 GB+. Excluding augur's runtime state and build artifacts keeps it to a few hundred bytes.

# augur runtime state (installed layout under ~/.augur)
vms/
claude-projects/
proxy/
*.img

# build artifacts (repo + staged sidecar source)
.build/
**/.build/

# vcs / editor cruft
.git/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
